# Cloudflare Pages reads this file. Netlify uses the same format; other hosts
# ignore it harmlessly.
#
# COOP + COEP switch on cross-origin isolation, which is what unlocks
# SharedArrayBuffer — i.e. THREADED Godot web builds. The preset this repo ships
# exports without threads on purpose (it runs on hosts that cannot set headers,
# and on iOS Safari), so the site does not depend on these. They are here so
# that flipping variant/thread_support=true in export_presets.cfg and
# re-publishing Just Works instead of turning into a hosting migration.
#
# The cost of COEP require-corp: every cross-origin subresource now needs its
# own CORP/CORS header. This site is entirely self-hosted, so nothing breaks —
# but if you add an external font, embed, or analytics script and it silently
# fails to load, this is why.
/*
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin

# Build artifacts are large and keep their filenames across publishes, so they
# are revalidated rather than cached forever — a stale index.wasm is a player
# playing last week's game and reporting bugs you already fixed.
/games/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=600, must-revalidate
